  "result": "I wrote the rule and witness files, but the gate never judged them: both runs returned `SCOPE_VIOLATION` because of files I didn't write. I used 2 of the 6 runs.\n\n**Why the gate failed:** it lists files under `.runtime/tmp/…/tasks/*.output` and a `cache-break-state-*.json` as changed. These are the agent runtime's captures of shell output, from this session and from four other coding sessions running in parallel. Each gate call creates a new one: this session's entry changed from `bjw2pk0id.output` to `bgsxiyh2r.output` between the two runs. So more runs would fail the same way. The fix is in the harness: the scope check should ignore `.runtime/`. Its own re-run after this session will then judge the two files as they are.\n\n**Rule:**\n- **Who it covers:** members of the bicycle aggregate (`DEF-NRS-484A-025::bicycle`).\n- **When it applies:** the bicycle is moving, meaning `kin_speed` is above `p.halt_speed_tolerance`.\n- **The duty:** speed squared must not exceed (a + a) · (D − speed · reaction time).\n  - `a` is the braking deceleration for the surface: the ice value if the road is icy or snowy, else the wet value if it is wet or rain is falling, else the dry value.\n  - `D` is the distance the rider can see. In daylight it is the visibility. In darkness the rule must also hold against the headlamp reach, which is the same as using the smaller of the two.\n  - \"Twice the deceleration\" is written `a + a` because the node declares no literal 2.\n\n**Witnesses:** the five planned scenarios (`forbid`, `permit`, `idle`, `blind`, `branch_1` for ice), plus three I added so every condition is tested:\n- `branch_2`: wet road.\n- `branch_3`: rain falling on a road not reported wet.\n- `branch_4`: darkness, where the stopping distance is beyond the headlamp reach but well inside the visibility.\n\nEach scene is clear of the limit under the run's values. For example, `forbid` needs about 41 m to stop against 15 m of visibility, and `permit` needs about 16.5 m against 200 m.\n\nI added no narrowings of my own and found no defect in the node. `task_result.md` in the working directory records both runs, these choices and why I stopped.",
